  "rulings": [
    {
      "comment": "Players can only respond once this spell has been cast and all its costs have been paid. No one can try to destroy the creature you sacrificed to prevent you from casting this spell.",
      "oracle_id": "0b67dff0-5bb7-44fe-a72b-d3b1a6c0ee72",
      "published_at": "2013-04-15",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You must sacrifice exactly one creature to cast this spell; you cannot cast it without sacrificing a creature, and you cannot sacrifice additional creatures.",
      "oracle_id": "0b67dff0-5bb7-44fe-a72b-d3b1a6c0ee72",
      "published_at": "2013-04-15",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Burning-Tree Emissary's ability isn't a mana ability. It uses the stack and can be responded to.",
      "oracle_id": "327d9679-0049-4401-8dab-e0fb362306bd",
      "published_at": "2017-03-14",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Players can only respond once this spell has been cast and all its costs have been paid. No one can try to destroy the creature you sacrificed to prevent you from casting this spell.",
      "oracle_id": "6385fd0d-256d-4400-9319-afa8170024db",
      "published_at": "2013-04-15",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You must sacrifice exactly one creature to cast this spell; you cannot cast it without sacrificing a creature, and you cannot sacrifice additional creatures.",
      "oracle_id": "6385fd0d-256d-4400-9319-afa8170024db",
      "published_at": "2013-04-15",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In the same vein, you can cast Pyretic Ritual only at a time when you could cast any other instant, not at a time when you could activate a mana ability. For example, you can’t cast Pyretic Ritual in the midst of casting another spell; you’d need to cast Pyretic Ritual first.",
      "oracle_id": "86ef6474-613f-41fb-931c-d4279b03ed99",
      "published_at": "2010-08-15",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Pyretic Ritual is not a mana ability and doesn’t behave like one. You cast it as a spell. It uses the stack. It can be responded to, and it can be countered.",
      "oracle_id": "86ef6474-613f-41fb-931c-d4279b03ed99",
      "published_at": "2010-08-15",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You choose which color or colors of mana to add before you draw a card.",
      "oracle_id": "89c83a6d-f6c8-4984-a888-0db62dfb93b1",
      "published_at": "2020-08-07",
      "source": "wotc"
    }
  ],
